... given the previous thread, you probably saw this coming.

I hate barbarians. My barbarians suffered many terrible fates. The
first died on Astral after exhausting his resources. Another lost all
of his AC to Destroy Armor and disenchanters. Yet another died to a
locust, then a cursed AoLS.

What was different about *this* barbarian?

Well, for one thing, Belkar had -51 AC and found a (1:2) wand of
wishing in the Minetown wand shop. For another, he had ten potions of
full healing, enough death wands and cockatrice eggs to kill a small
army, and he took no chances with powerful opponents. Rodney got the
wand of death, which usually hit since I wore +5 Gauntlets of
Dexteriy. The demon lords, being immune to wands of death, got egg in
the face.

And he took no chances with the ascension run. He always had multiple
wands of death/teleportation in open inventory. He fooproofed armor
before waking Rodney. And most importantly, he had scrolls of gold
detection written well in advance.

Finally, he indirectly found his *own bones pile* full of stoning
grenades and a wand of wishing (1:2) (that he never even *needed*).
See, after the previous incarnation of Belkar died in the Valley, some
guy found his stuff, descended way too quickly, and got smashed to
bits by Asmodeus. When I opened his bag of holding, sure enough, there
were the cockatrice eggs painstakingly laid by the previous Belkar.

Aside from that, the only real noteworthy accomplishments were
creating some assorted +9 weapons for #twoweaponing, and level-
draining *myself* with Stormy after raiding Ludios to get all 20
points of divine protection. :) Truth be told, Stormy hurt like hell,
but it wasn't difficult to regain the lost levels since I tried this
just after finishing the castle.

All in all, I still hate barbarians. But I feel a little better now
that I got one upstairs. =)


